	(text "Click a box on the left to open its page. \"Contents\" and the page\nnumbers at the bottom right of every page lead back here and to each page.\n\nCyan lines are connections: wires and pin ends, all one width.\nA dot joins lines; a cross on a pin end means the pin is not connected.\nPins connect by net labels (the boxed names): pins whose labels carry\nthe same name are on one net, on any page.\n[3/C4] after a label: page 3 carries that net too, its label in zone C4\n(column 4, row C of the border). Click it to land on that label.\nNo [page/zone]: the net is on this page only.\nClick a part's reference to find its row in the parts list; the row's\npage/zone leads back. A part crossed out in red is not fitted (DNP).\nWhite: parts and their references. Grey: values, pin names, pin numbers.\nA dashed frame is a block of the circuit, titled at its top left.\nAn amber K3 marks a Kleidos addition or correction: it leads to its row below."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 45.085 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c9df4a98-dfe8-56bf-81f8-2fd49e7d029d")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 96.06 0)
		(effects
